# Project flow templates

Templates live in `libs/project_templates/*.json`. The loader derives `preview_nodes` / `preview_edges` automatically — do not add them to JSON.

## JSON schema

```json
{
  "id": "kebab-case-id",         // also the filename stem
  "name": "Human readable name",
  "summary": "One-line description shown in template grid",
  "description": "Longer paragraph shown in detail view",
  "category": "scrape|agent|data|infra|general",
  "category_label": "Human label",
  "tags": ["tag1", "tag2"],
  "author": "Cross-Border",
  "featured": false,
  "nodes": [ /* ProjectNode objects */ ],
  "edges": [ /* ProjectEdge objects */ ]
}
```

## Node structure

```json
{
  "id": "n-unique-id",
  "kind": "schedule|webhook|scrape|agent|export|condition|notify|postgres|redis|github|sticky",
  "role": "trigger|action|agent|config|note",
  "label": "Display name",
  "subtitle": "Secondary line (cron, platform, condition expression, etc.)",
  "status": "online",
  "x": 60,   // canvas x — increment 220-260px per step
  "y": 240,  // base y; branch up -80..100 / down +80..120 for forks
  "pluginId": "1688",           // scrape nodes only
  "pluginProfile": "scraper-1688",
  "agentPrompt": "...",         // agent nodes
  "options": { "key": "value" } // optionKey values from node-config schemas
}
```

**Role defaults by kind:**

| Kind | Default role |
|------|-------------|
| `webhook`, `schedule` | `trigger` |
| `agent` | `agent` |
| `sticky` | `note` |
| everything else | `action` |

## Edge structure

```json
{ "id": "e-from-to", "from": "n-from-id", "to": "n-to-id", "kind": "main" }
```

- `kind: "main"` for workflow connections; `kind: "config"` for sub-node (plugin/model) wiring
- Fan-out from a `condition` node is valid: one edge per branch target
- All `from` and `to` must reference IDs that exist in `nodes`

## Canvas layout conventions

| Pattern | x gap | y offset |
|---------|-------|----------|
| Linear chain | +220–260 | same y |
| Branch up (success) | same x | −100 to −120 |
| Branch down (fail/alt) | same x | +100 to +140 |
| Sticky note (below) | 60–300 | +180–220 below lowest node |

Start first node at `x: 60, y: 220`.

## Available node kinds & typical options

| Kind | Common options |
|------|----------------|
| `schedule` | subtitle: `"cron: 0 8 * * *"` |
| `webhook` | `options.webhookActive: true`, subtitle: `"POST /hooks/..."` |
| `scrape` | `pluginId`, `options.plugin_id`, `options.ai_extraction`, `options.batch_mode` |
| `agent` | `agentPrompt` (multi-line string) |
| `condition` | subtitle: condition expression, e.g. `"items.length > 0"` |
| `export` | `options.exportTarget: "shopee"`, `options.dryRun: true` |
| `notify` | `options.integrateChannel: "telegram"`, `options.level: "info|warning|error"` |
| `postgres` | `options.dbName`, `options.username`, `options.port: "5432"` |
| `redis` | `options.port: "6379"`, `options.dbIndex: "0"` |
| `sticky` | `noteBody`, `noteColor: "blue|green|yellow|red|purple"`, `noteWidth`, `noteHeight` |

## Categories in use

| id | label |
|----|-------|
| `scrape` | Scrape pipeline |
| `agent` | Agent automation |
| `data` | Data pipeline |
| `infra` | Infrastructure |
| `general` | General |

## Validation

After adding/editing a template, run:

```bash
python -c "
import json, pathlib, sys
for f in pathlib.Path('libs/project_templates').glob('*.json'):
    d = json.loads(f.read_text())
    ids = {n['id'] for n in d.get('nodes',[])}
    for e in d.get('edges',[]):
        assert e['from'] in ids, f'{f.name}: bad edge from {e[\"from\"]}'
        assert e['to'] in ids, f'{f.name}: bad edge to {e[\"to\"]}'
    print('OK', f.name)
"
```
